From b3abc77dc9ebc84891ec685424bfd96c320273ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:48:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Narration plugin: audio per slide, per language and
 variant, from any static server
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

resources/narration.js (+ narration.css) is a reveal plugin. A slide embeds
the NAME of a recording in a tag — data-narration="<name>" on the section,
on any element inside it, or on a fragment (played when it shows) — and the
plugin plays <base>/<name>.<lang>[.<variant>].<format>, trying the deck's
variant first and falling back to the plain file, so a deck can re-record a
few slides and share the rest. Slides are not named: the name is the
recording's and goes with the slide into every deck it is built into.

A floating panel (draggable by its header, collapsible, place and language
remembered in localStorage) carries the language buttons, play / pause, a
seek bar and `auto` — "hear me talk": every recording ends on Reveal.next(),
a slide without one lasts `silentDelay` ms, and auto stops on the last
slide. Keys pressed in the panel never reach the deck. Configured in
Reveal.initialize({ narration: { base, langs, lang, variant, format,
silentDelay, auto, panel } }); base null = plugin off;
?narration=<base>&lang=en&variant=x override without rebuilding.

src/slides/mental-model-llm.html names its 34 recordings
mental-model/<slug> and mental-model-of-llms.html loads the plugin with
base null (set it, or try a server with ?narration=). claude-on-scotch
rebuilds with the attributes, its e2e golden is unchanged.

tests/e2e/narration.test.js drives a fixture deck against silent WAVs the
test server makes up: variant fallback, auto mode through fragments and a
silent slide, language switch, play on one slide, the panel's drag /
collapse / persistence. tests/e2e/server.js is the static server both e2e
files share.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
